{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A player five minutes into their first room will type "},{"code":"attack the chair","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"smell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"listen"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"climb the ladder"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"jump","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"dig","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"buy lamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". None of those is a verb","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most games implement. All of them are verbs every player tries.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"I don't know the word \"attack\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" answers the wrong question. It says the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"program","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" is unfinished. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Attacking the chair rarely improves matters."},{"type":"text","text":" says the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"world","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is — and the player learns something from the second answer and nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the first."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So the engine ships about fifty of these words with a line of stock prose each."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Nothing about them is a special case in the parser. A stub verb is an ordinary"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row in the standard table whose intent happens to have no mechanic behind it,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which means it:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Is in the vocabulary"}]},{"text":", so it is never ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"I don't know the word"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Resolves its objects through normal scope."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"attack the grue","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is no grue still answers ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"“You can’t see any such thing.”","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" A stub doesn’t buy","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"politeness by weakening scope honesty.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Scope is the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"visible"}]},{"type":"text","text":" set, which admits what can be seen through the glass"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a shut jar or in somebody else’s hands — so the physical stubs re-check"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reach"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and refuse with "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/cantReach","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", exactly as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"push"},{"type":"text","text":" does."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Through the shut bottle in Zork’s kitchen, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"push water"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"squeeze water"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"burn water"},{"type":"text","text":" now all answer "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“You can’t reach the quantity of water.”"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"opening the bottle lets all three through."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Which verbs check is a call made per verb, because a blanket guard would be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrong: ","type":"text"},{"code":"smell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"listen to","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"point at","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"buy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"sell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wake"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"are fine at a distance — you can smell a fire across a room, count coins","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"behind glass, and shout somebody awake. ","type":"text"},{"code":"throw … at …","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" checks the projectile","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and deliberately not the target, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"give … to …","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the one stub that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checks both slots, since handing something over is contact with the gift and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with whoever takes it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs a turn."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" Flailing at the chair takes time; fuses and daemons tick."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This is the substantive difference from the parse error it replaces, which was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"free."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Is overridable at every layer, with no warning","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — because overriding is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the expected end state, not a mistake."}]}]}],"type":"orderedList"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Whats-in-the-set","type":"heading","text":"What’s in the set"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Violence and force: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"attack"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kill"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"hit","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"fight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (bare or ","type":"text"},{"code":"with","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" a weapon),","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"break","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"smash","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"destroy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"burn","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"cut","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"dig","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"pull","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"drag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"turn","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"rotate","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"squeeze","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shake"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"knock (on)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throw … at …"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Senses: "},{"code":"touch","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"feel","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"rub","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"smell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"sniff","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"listen (to)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"taste","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"lick","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Body: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"eat"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"drink"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sleep"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"wake (up)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Social: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kiss"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hug"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"give","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hand … to …"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"yell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"shout","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"scream","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"wave","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"point at","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Motion: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"climb (up\/down\/on)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"jump (over)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swim"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dive"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stand (up)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sit (down\/on)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lie (down)"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kneel"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Liquids and containers: "},{"code":"fill","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"pour","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tie"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"untie"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Ritual and flavor: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pray"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sing"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"curse"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swear"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"xyzzy"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plugh"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"think","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"wish","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Commerce: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"buy"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sell"},{"type":"text","text":". Fixtures: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"blow"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Deliberately ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" stubs: ","type":"text"},{"code":"again","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"oops","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"verbose"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"brief"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"notify","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"script"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"are missing ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"features","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", and a canned refusal would be a worse answer than the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"error. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ask"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tell"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"show"},{"text":" belong to ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoConversation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which has a topic slot","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and somebody to ask. Bare "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hello"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"hi","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"ring","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"wind","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are left free for games","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that want to own them outright."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Aimed-at-yourself","text":"Aimed at yourself"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The player is an entity, and it is called “yourself” — so a stub line that names"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its object would read "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"“The yourself is not food.”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Every name-carrying stub"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checks for the player and answers "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies\/yourself"},{"text":" instead.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Stubs whose lines name nothing keep their own answer, because it already reads","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"correctly: ","type":"text"},{"code":"taste me","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" still says ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“You’d rather not.”"}],"type":"emphasis"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Eighteen of them are handed an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"optional"}]},{"type":"text","text":" name, and either of two things puts"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a verb there. Some have rows that carry no object at all — "},{"code":"smell","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"smell the troll","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are one intent — so one sentence has to read both ways. The rest fill the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slot on every row but read perfectly well with the name left out: "},{"code":"knock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"taste"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kiss"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"count"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"buy"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sell"},{"text":" are about the player as much as the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"thing, so the name is offered rather than required.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The player takes the nameless half rather than the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"yourself"},{"type":"text","text":" deferral, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same answer by a different road: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"smell me"},{"type":"text","text":" still says "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"“You smell nothing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out of the ordinary.”"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Seventeen of the eighteen also skip the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"somebodyElse"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guard, and that follows from the shape rather than being a convenience — a line"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"with a nameless half is a line that can be said about anybody. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"touch"},{"text":" is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one that keeps it, because laying hands on somebody is not the same as listening","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to them; ","type":"text"},{"code":"kiss","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the one that shows why the call is per verb, since kissing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"somebody is what the verb is ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"for","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Re-skinning-a-line","level":2,"text":"Re-skinning a line"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every stub line lives on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/stubs"},{"text":", one property per intent. Override","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the ones that clash with your voice and leave the rest:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var text: GameText {","    var text = GameText()","    text.stubs.attack = .naming { \"The Institute frowns on assaulting \\($0).\" }","    text.stubs.pray = \"No one is listening. You checked.\"","    return text","}"]},{"text":"Promoting a stub to real behavior","type":"heading","anchor":"Promoting-a-stub-to-real-behavior","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This is the part that makes the whole design worth it: the parser already knows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"the word, so a game only has to add a rule. No "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#verb"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entry, no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"warning. Zork’s climbable tree is one line:"}]},{"code":["tree.before(.climb) {","    try reply(Prose.treeClimb)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For behavior that spans every object rather than one, use an "},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" row —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" turns the whole "},{"code":"attack","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" family into real combat that way:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["public var actions: [IntentAction] {","    action(.attack) {","        try reply(","            text.attackFutile(command.directObject?.indefiniteNoun ?? GameText.Noun(\"that\")))","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"anchor":"To-change-only-the-words-assign-the-line","type":"heading","text":"To change only the words, assign the line"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" row replaces the stub’s ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"whole","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" default, and the reach guard is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"part of that default: ","type":"text"},{"code":"DefaultActions.run","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" returns from an override before it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"calls ","type":"text"},{"code":"requireReach","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", because a game that claims the verb is saying it will","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decide for itself what “close enough to touch” means. ","type":"text"},{"code":"GnustoMeleeCombat","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" wants","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly that.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A game that only wants a different sentence does not, and gets it anyway. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"re-voicing is an assignment, not a row — and the assignment is a sentence:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var text: GameText {","    var text = GameText()","    text.stubs.climb = \"That is not something you could climb.\"","    return text","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A line that ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"does","type":"text"}]},{"text":" want to name what the player pointed at says so, in the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slot:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["text.stubs.climb = .naming(orBare: \"There's nothing here worth climbing.\") {","    \"You can't climb onto \\($0).\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both halves, because a line that owns a nameless half has two things to say and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"writing only one leaves the engine’s narrator answering the other. See","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The assignment keeps the reach guard, the object’s rendered name, its number","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"agreement, and the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies\/yourself","type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies\/somebodyElse","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" guards — and, since wanting the name is","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"now something an assignment can do, it has stopped being a reason to reach for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row at all. The row keeps none of them, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nothing warns — a row and an assignment look equally reasonable at the call site."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Dungeon\/"},{"type":"text","text":" re-skinned seventeen stubs with rows and had given all four"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"away without noticing."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rule of thumb:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actions"},{"type":"text","text":" row means "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"this game has behavior here"}]},{"type":"text","text":". If"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all it has is a sentence, assign the sentence."}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Use-reply-not-say","text":"Use `reply`, not `say`","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The stage-4 default ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"says","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" its line rather than refusing, so world time passes on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a stub turn. That means a ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rule which only ","type":"text"},{"code":"say","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s does ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" suppress","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the stock line — the player gets both. Promote a stub with ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/reply(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":", which end the turn.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Precedence","text":"Precedence","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not “item beats room”. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"},{"type":"text","text":" rules run outside-in, so whoever "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reply"},{"type":"text","text":"s or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refuse"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"first","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" wins:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"World ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Location "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"beforeEachTurn"},{"type":"text","text":", then location "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Item ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — indirect object, then direct object","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The game’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" row for that intent","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The engine’s stub line","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"So a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"world.before(.dig)"},{"type":"text","text":" pre-empts a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sand.before(.dig)"},{"type":"text","text":". See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"text":"Reclaiming the word entirely","type":"heading","anchor":"Reclaiming-the-word-entirely","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you want the ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"word","type":"text"}]},{"text":" to mean something else, claim its row. Reclaiming a stub","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row is silent, unlike reclaiming a core row:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var verbs: [SyntaxRule] {","    SyntaxRule(\"attack\", .directObject, intent: Intent(\"brawl\"))","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Notes for engine work","type":"heading","anchor":"Notes-for-engine-work","level":2},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table is split: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreTable"},{"type":"text","text":" is the rows with real behavior,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"stubTable"},{"type":"text","text":" is these, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"standardTable"},{"type":"text","text":" is both. Bootstrap keys"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its override warning off "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreTable"},{"type":"text","text":", and that split "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"is"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the stub flag."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A stub’s intent, rows and line are one "},{"code":"StubVerb","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, so a stub can’t be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"half-declared — rows with no line would fall through to stage 4’s last resort,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so a word the engine advertises would answer “You can’t do that.” Core verbs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have the same shape for the same reason: a ","type":"text"},{"code":"CoreVerb","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an intent, its rows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and its handler, and both tables and both intent sets are derived from those","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two arrays rather than restated.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Stub intents are deliberately ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"code":"DefaultActions.builtInIntents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is what keeps ","type":"text"},{"code":"action(.dig)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" from warning. ","type":"text"},{"code":"handledIntents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the union, used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for the dead-intent check. ","type":"text"},{"code":"engineIntents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is the third set — UNDO, RESTART,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"SAVE and RESTORE, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"GameWorld.run","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" answers before the pipeline — and an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actions"},{"type":"text","text":" row for one of those warns that it can never run."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No stub row uses a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".topic"},{"type":"text","text":" slot, and none should. A topic never fails to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match, so a low-specificity topic row silently absorbs the scope failures of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every more specific row sharing its verb word — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"say hello to butler"},{"type":"text","text":" with no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"butler present would answer a canned line instead of “You can’t see any such"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thing.”"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A bare ","type":"text"},{"code":"verb <object>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" row suppresses the ","type":"text"},{"code":"missingIndirect","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" prompt from any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"verb <object> PREP <second object>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" row on the same verb word, because the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"parser returns on the first row that ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"matches"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" and only falls back to a","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"near-miss when nothing matched. That is why "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"give"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throw"},{"type":"text","text":" ship"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second-object-only: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"give lamp"},{"type":"text","text":" asking "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"“What do you want to give the lamp","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to?”","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" beats a canned line."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"level":2,"text":"See also","type":"heading","anchor":"See-also"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","isActive":true}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextAndRandomness"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"Stub Verbs","modules":[{"name":"Gnusto"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/StubVerbs","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Verbs and Intents","anchor":"Verbs-and-Intents","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/verb(_:_:)","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SyntaxRule","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SyntaxElement","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IntentAction","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Topic"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto\/stubverbs"]}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto"],["doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapDiagnostics"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The verbs the parser knows as words even where your game has no mechanic.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/IntentAction":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IntentAction","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IntentAction"}],"title":"IntentAction","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/IntentAction","abstract":[{"text":"A replacement or new stage-4 default action for one intent — the seam","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that lets a game or plugin give a custom verb real behavior instead of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"“I didn’t understand”, or replace a built-in’s default entirely.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/intentaction","type":"topic"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/SyntaxRule":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One row of the verb table: a pattern of literal words and slots, and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"intent a match produces. Data, not code — games can add rows through their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"verbs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" block to teach the parser new player-typeable verbs."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SyntaxRule","title":"SyntaxRule","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SyntaxRule","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/syntaxrule","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SyntaxRule","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TextAndRandomness":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Text and Randomness","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TextAndRandomness","abstract":[{"text":"Re-skin the engine’s stock lines, and roll dice that replay.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/textandrandomness"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/TheTurnPipeline":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/theturnpipeline","abstract":[{"text":"What happens between the player pressing Return and the next prompt.","type":"text"}],"title":"The Turn Pipeline","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/TheTurnPipeline","kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/cantReach":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"cantReach"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4LineV","text":"Line"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4NounV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Noun"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/cantreach","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/cantReach","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The item resolved (it was visible to the parser), but a reachability"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"guard failed — you can see it, you just can’t touch it (e.g. through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shut glass jar). Distinct from "},{"code":"cantSeeAnySuchThing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is for a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"noun that isn’t in scope at all."}],"title":"cantReach"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/verb(_:_:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"verb","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", [","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto13SyntaxElementO","text":"SyntaxElement","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]...)","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/verb(_:_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Declares a custom player-typeable verb in one place: a typed intent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constant plus the verb rows that produce it.","type":"text"}],"title":"verb(_:_:)","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/verb(_:_:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/SyntaxElement":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SyntaxElement"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SyntaxElement"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/syntaxelement","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One element of a verb pattern: a literal word the player must type, or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"slot the parser fills from the rest of the sentence. String literals in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pattern are "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".word"},{"type":"text","text":"s, so rows read the way they’re typed:"}],"title":"SyntaxElement","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/SyntaxElement","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/StubReplies/yourself":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"yourself","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4LineV","text":"Line","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV7NothingV","text":"Nothing","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A stub verb aimed at yourself, where the verb’s own line would have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"named its object. The player item is called “yourself”, so those","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lines would read “The yourself is not food.” — one line covers all of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them rather than fifteen self-specific variants.","type":"text"}],"title":"yourself","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/stubreplies\/yourself","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies\/yourself"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/StubReplies/somebodyElse":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"somebodyElse"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4LineV","text":"Line"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV","text":"GameText"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV4NounV","text":"Noun","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"somebodyElse","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A stub verb aimed at somebody else, where the verb would otherwise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have reported a completed act on a person — “The cook is not food.”,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“You feel nothing out of the ordinary.” about a witness. Every stub"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that has to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reach"}]},{"type":"text","text":" its object goes through this, so one line covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all of them, the way "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies\/yourself","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" does."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/stubreplies\/somebodyelse","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/StubReplies\/somebodyElse"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/Topic":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/Topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Topic","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Topic","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"Topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/topic","abstract":[{"text":"What the player wants to talk about: the words after “about”, normalized","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the way the parser normalizes everything else — lowercased, punctuation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"dropped, filler stripped.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/reply(_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/reply(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"reply"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Never","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO"}],"title":"reply(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/reply(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Fully handles the current action with a response, skipping the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"behavior. Mechanically identical to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refuse(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" — two names exist so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"game code reads correctly: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refuse"},{"type":"text","text":" for “no, you can’t”, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reply"},{"type":"text","text":" for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“here’s what happens instead”."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/Line":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Line","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Line"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/line","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/Line","title":"GameText.Line","abstract":[{"text":"One stock line, in whichever shape the game wants it: a fixed sentence,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a sentence assembled when it prints, or one that names the thing it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"about."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/BootstrapDiagnostics":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/bootstrapdiagnostics","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every message the bootstrap can print, and what to change."}],"title":"Bootstrap Diagnostics","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/BootstrapDiagnostics","kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/AddingCustomVerbs":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/addingcustomverbs","abstract":[{"text":"Teach the parser words the built-in table doesn’t know.","type":"text"}],"title":"Adding Custom Verbs","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/AddingCustomVerbs","kind":"article"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/refuse(_:)":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/refuse(_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refuse"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s5NeverO","text":"Never"}],"title":"refuse(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/refuse(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"Blocks the current action with a complaint. The default action and any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"remaining ","type":"text"},{"code":"before","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"after","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rules are skipped; world time still passes.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto":{"type":"topic","title":"Gnusto","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"An engine for writing interactive fiction in Swift.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/GameText/stubs":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"stubs","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GameText","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto8GameTextV11StubRepliesV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"StubReplies"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/gametext\/stubs","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The stock replies for the verbs the parser knows as words but the engine"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"gives no mechanic. Re-skin one with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"text.stubs.dig = \"…\""},{"type":"text","text":"; give one real"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"behavior with a rule or an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"actions"},{"type":"text","text":" row."}],"title":"stubs","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/GameText\/stubs","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Gnusto/documentation/Gnusto/WritingRules":{"url":"\/documentation\/gnusto\/writingrules","identifier":"doc:\/\/Gnusto\/documentation\/Gnusto\/WritingRules","abstract":[{"text":"Attach game logic to items, locations, and the world.","type":"text"}],"title":"Writing Rules","type":"topic","kind":"article","role":"article"}}}